    <div><p class="eyebrow">Start with a question</p><h2 id="research-title">Study work in context</h2></div>
    <div class="prose"><p>Research is most useful when it begins with a decision, not a preferred method. Clarify what the team needs to learn and who has relevant experience.</p><p>In scientific settings, pay attention to data, tools, handoffs, environmental constraints, and the differences between documented and actual practice.</p></div>
  </div>
