<section class="section tinted-section" aria-labelledby="research-tools-title"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading section-heading--compact"><div><p class="eyebrow">Core activities</p><h2 id="research-tools-title">Build trustworthy evidence</h2></div><p>Use multiple forms of evidence when the decision or consequence warrants it.</p></div><div class="card-grid">
  <article class="content-card"><p class="card-number">01</p><h3>Plan</h3><p>Define the question, participants, ethics, constraints, and how findings will inform a decision.</p></article>
  <article class="content-card"><p class="card-number">02</p><h3>Observe</h3><p>Use interviews, contextual inquiry, and workflow mapping to learn from behavior and context.</p></article>
  <article class="content-card"><p class="card-number">03</p><h3>Synthesize</h3><p>Separate observation from interpretation, show patterns and exceptions, and state limitations plainly.</p></article>
